]
},
{
"tag": "div",
"children": [
{
"tag": "div",
"children": [
{
"tag": "h4",
"children": [
"Educational Fee Waivers"
]
},
{
"tag": "p",
"children": [
"National Park Service policy permits entrance fees to be waived for national and international academic institutions visiting parks for non-commercial educational purposes. However, Educational Fee Waivers are not issued automatically. Educational groups must apply and meet the criteria to receive a fee waiver.",
{
"tag": "a",
"href": "/grca/planyourvisit/educational-fee-waiver.htm",
"children": [
"How to qualify for and apply for an Educational Fee Waiver"
]
}
]
}
]
},
{
"tag": "div",
"children": [
{
"tag": "p",
"children": [
{
"tag": "strong",
"children": [
"Organized Non-commercial Groups include:"
]
}
]
},
{
"tag": "ul",
"children": [
{
"tag": "li",
"children": [
"Church groups"
]
},
{
"tag": "li",
"children": [
"College/school clubs and organizations"
]
},
{
"tag": "li",
"children": [
"Large Girl Scout, Boy Scout and other youth groups"
]
},
{
"tag": "li",
"children": [
"Service organizations, etc."
]
}
]
},
{
"tag": "p",
"children": [
"Organized Non-commercial Groups in vehicles with a manufacture's designed capacity of 16 or less are charged the $35.00 vehicle permit or a fee of $8.00 per person in vehicles with a manufacture's designed capacity of 16 or greater. Age and pass exemptions apply.",
{
"tag": "a",
"href": "/grca/planyourvisit/org_non_commercial.htm",
"children": [
"Find the best option for your group"
]
}
]
}
]
},
{
"tag": "div",
"children": [
{
"tag": "p",
"children": [
"A",
{
"tag": "a",
"href": "/grca/getinvolved/cua.htm",
"children": [
"Commercial Use Authorization"
]
},
{
"tag": "strong",
"children": [
"(CUA)"
]
},
"is required for any commercial tour company, regional shuttle service company, or local transit company that enters the park.",
{
"tag": "strong",
"children": [
"Commercial Vehicles must show their CUA upon",
{
"tag": "u",
"children": [
"every"
]
},
"entry to Grand Canyon National Park."
]
},
{
"tag": "strong",
"children": [
"Grand Canyon National Park only accepts credit or debit cards for all entrance fees, including commercial tour fees."
]
},
"No Golden Eagle, Golden Age, Golden Access, Grand Canyon Park Passes, or America the Beautiful – National Parks and Federal Recreational Lands Passes, will be accepted and there are no exemptions for age."
]
},
{
"tag": "ul",
"children": [
{
"tag": "li",
"children": [
{
"tag": "strong",
"children": [
"Vehicles with capacity of 1-25:"
]
},
"will be charged a Flat Fee of $8.00 per person. Those age 15 and under will be exempt from payment of fees."
]
},
{
"tag": "li",
"children": [
{
"tag": "strong",
"children": [
"Vehicles with capacity of 26 or greater:"
]
},
"will be charged a flat fee of $300.00."
]
},
{
"tag": "li",
"children": [
{
"tag": "strong",
"children": [
"Clients entering in their own vehicle in vehicle caravan or meet guide in the park:"
]
},
"In any instance where the clients enter the park in their own vehicle, each vehicle will be charged the regular, single-vehicle fee ($30 Motorcycles, $35 Vehicle). If one or more group members own an America The Beautiful: Federal Lands Pass, each pass will be accepted for entry of one vehicle."
]
}
]
},
{
"tag": "p",
"children": [
{
"tag": "a",
"href": "/grca/planyourvisit/com_tour_fees.htm",
"children": [
